# squads/<squad-id>.md template (design 5.9)
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-10-29 — branch= names the landing branch; row format unchanged
# Process version: 2026-10-29.1
# Current process: root CLAUDE.md (Subagent Workflow), plus the planning skill's
# knowledge/coordination-ledger.md. The strict row format below is unchanged.
# Every row uses lead=team-lead: a separate independent stream is a separate
# team-lead session, and there is no squad-lead role.
# branch= names the landing branch (landing/<train>, or a standalone
# feature's own landing branch); there are no work-package branches.
#
# One canonical file per feature/train/independent stream (for example
# squads/security-hardening.md). Updated on every status change by the
# stream's own session — "The stream's own file; updated on every status
# change". Claims are planning information, not machine locks; resolve duplicate
# area owners with the chief before dispatch. Only HOLDS.md and
# LANDING-LOCK are mechanically enforced (by the pre-push hook).
#
# Row format (one line — the design calls this "one squad's row"):
#
#   squad=<squad-id> | session=<session-id-or-in-session> | lead=<role> | worktree=<absolute-path> | branch=<branch-name> | claim=<trees-or-files> | status=<planned|in-flight|gated|handed-back|waiting-for-founder|landed|blocked|released> | last-updated=<ISO8601> by <who>
#
# scripts/dev-machine-capacity.sh counts active dispatches by grepping this
# directory for "status=in-flight" — keep the field name and value exactly
# as shown (case-sensitive, no extra spaces around "=") or the capacity
# monitor will undercount.
#
# A pending landing announcement is appended below the row as a second line
# (design: "The row also carries the squad's landing announcements when one
# is pending") and removed once the landing lock is released and the
# landing is posted to LANDING-LOG.md:
#
#   LANDING-ANNOUNCEMENT squad=<squad-id> branch=<branch-name> announced-at=<ISO8601> by=<who>
#
# The stream's GOAL is its own line below the row (never a row field — goal
# text may contain "|"), written by whoever starts the stream and kept until
# the stream is landed or released; no parser reads it:
#
#   GOAL squad=<squad-id> set-at=<ISO8601> by=<who> :: <end state, one line>
#
# A row untouched for 2 hours with no live session behind it is "stale"
# (G3) — the chief asks the founder before releasing or re-assigning it.
#
# Example (illustration only — replace <squad-id> in the filename and every
# field below):
# squad=security-hardening | session=separate-session-2 | lead=team-lead | worktree=/Users/danielpiatkowski/AI-Agent-Workspace/omnipus/wt-security-hardening | branch=landing/security-hardening | claim=pkg/auth/, pkg/fspolicy/ | status=in-flight | last-updated=2026-09-25T09:05:00Z by team-lead
